claims:
1. A method in a computer system for identifying importance of blocks to a primary topic of a page that contains the blocks, the method comprising:
providing a collection of training pages with blocks;
for each block of a training page with non-noise information,
generating a feature vector that represents the block; and
collecting from a person an indication of relative importance of the block to the primary topic of its page;

learning a function from the generated feature vector and the indicated importance of each block that represents a mapping from feature vector to importance; and
applying the learned function to a feature vector representation of the blocks of the page to generate an indication of the relative importance of each block to a primary topic of the page.
